{"content":[{"c":["ELEAZAR"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Third of Aaron’s four sons (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.6.23","r":"Exod.6.23","rawR":"Exod.6.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.6.23","value":"Exod.6.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 6:23"},"). Eleazar (“God has helped”) was consecrated as a priest with his brothers and Aaron in the Sinai (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.28.1","r":"Exod.28.1","rawR":"Exod.28.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.28.1","value":"Exod.28.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 28:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.8.2,13","r":"Lev.8.2,13","rawR":"Lev.8.2,13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.8.2,13","value":"Lev.8.2,13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 8:2, 13"},"). When his brothers Nadab and Abihu were killed by God as they offered “unholy fire” to the Lord (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.10.1-7","r":"Lev.10.1-7","rawR":"Lev.10.1-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.10.1-7","value":"Lev.10.1-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 10:1-7"},"), Eleazar and Ithamar took leading positions as Aaron’s sons (",{"href":"?bref=Num.3.1-4","r":"Num.3.1-4","rawR":"Num.3.1-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.3.1-4","value":"Num.3.1-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 3:1-4"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["Eleazar is described as “chief of the leaders of the Levites” (",{"href":"?bref=Num.3.32","r":"Num.3.32","rawR":"Num.3.32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.3.32","value":"Num.3.32"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 3:32"},"). Under his supervision were the sanctuary and its vessels (",{"href":"?bref=Num.4.16","r":"Num.4.16","rawR":"Num.4.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.4.16","value":"Num.4.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.16.37-39","r":"Num.16.37-39","rawR":"Num.16.37-39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.16.37-39","value":"Num.16.37-39"}],"t":"ref","v":"16:37-39"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.19.3-4","r":"Num.19.3-4","rawR":"Num.19.3-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.19.3-4","value":"Num.19.3-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:3-4"},"). Eleazar was installed as high priest by Moses when Aaron died on Mt Hor (",{"href":"?bref=Num.20.25-28","r":"Num.20.25-28","rawR":"Num.20.25-28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.20.25-28","value":"Num.20.25-28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 20:25-28"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.10.6","r":"Deut.10.6","rawR":"Deut.10.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.10.6","value":"Deut.10.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 10:6"},"). He was then considered Moses’ assistant (",{"href":"?bref=Num.26.1-3,63","r":"Num.26.1-3,63","rawR":"Num.26.1-3,63","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.26.1-3,63","value":"Num.26.1-3,63"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 26:1-3, 63"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.27.2,21","r":"Num.27.2,21","rawR":"Num.27.2,21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.27.2,21","value":"Num.27.2,21"}],"t":"ref","v":"27:2, 21"},"). Joshua was commissioned by Moses in the presence of Eleazar (",{"href":"?bref=Num.27.18-23","r":"Num.27.18-23","rawR":"Num.27.18-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.27.18-23","value":"Num.27.18-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"27:18-23"},"). In the conquest of Canaan, Joshua and Eleazar served together as leaders. It was Eleazar’s function as Joshua’s counselor to inquire of the Lord (v ",{"href":"?bref=Num.27.21","r":"Num.27.21","rawR":"Num.27.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.27.21","value":"Num.27.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"21"},"). He also had his share in the census taking at Shittim. He took part in the partitioning of Canaan, the east bank (",{"href":"?bref=Num.34.17","r":"Num.34.17","rawR":"Num.34.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.34.17","value":"Num.34.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"34:17"},"), and the west bank (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.14.1","r":"Josh.14.1","rawR":"Josh.14.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.14.1","value":"Josh.14.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 14:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.17.4","r":"Josh.17.4","rawR":"Josh.17.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.17.4","value":"Josh.17.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"17:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.51","r":"Josh.19.51","rawR":"Josh.19.51","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.51","value":"Josh.19.51"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:51"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.1","r":"Josh.21.1","rawR":"Josh.21.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.1","value":"Josh.21.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":["When Eleazar died, he was highly regarded and memorialized in the land of Ephraim (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.24.33","r":"Josh.24.33","rawR":"Josh.24.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.24.33","value":"Josh.24.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 24:33"},"); his son Phinehas followed him as high priest."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":["In the oversight of the priests, 16 divisions were assigned to Eleazar’s descendants and eight to Ithamar’s (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.24.1-31","r":"1Chr.24.1-31","rawR":"1Chr.24.1-31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.24.1-31","value":"1Chr.24.1-31"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 24"},"). The ancestry of the prominent priests Zadok and Ezra is traced to Eleazar (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.3-15,50-53","r":"1Chr.6.3-15,50-53","rawR":"1Chr.6.3-15,50-53","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.3-15,50-53","value":"1Chr.6.3-15,50-53"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:3-15, 50-53"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.24.3","r":"1Chr.24.3","rawR":"1Chr.24.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.24.3","value":"1Chr.24.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"24:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.7.1-5","r":"Ezra.7.1-5","rawR":"Ezra.7.1-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.7.1-5","value":"Ezra.7.1-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 7:1-5"},"). In King Solomon’s time the priests of Zadok replaced Abiathar, a descendant of Ithamar (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.2.26-27,35","r":"1Kgs.2.26-27,35","rawR":"1Kgs.2.26-27,35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.2.26-27,35","value":"1Kgs.2.26-27,35"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 2:26-27, 35"},"). The descendants of Eleazar would be the only ones permitted to minister in Ezekiel’s ideal temple (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.44.15","r":"Ezek.44.15","rawR":"Ezek.44.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.44.15","value":"Ezek.44.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 44:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Aaron_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Aaron_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Aaron_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Aaron"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Abinadab’s son, charged with caring for the ark by the people of Kiriath-jearim, when it was brought from Beth-shemesh and placed in the “house of Abinadab on the hill” (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.7.1","r":"1Sam.7.1","rawR":"1Sam.7.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.7.1","value":"1Sam.7.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 7:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Dodo’s son, one of the three mighty men whose exploits against the Philistines gained him great fame (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.9","r":"2Sam.23.9","rawR":"2Sam.23.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.9","value":"2Sam.23.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 23:9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.12","r":"1Chr.11.12","rawR":"1Chr.11.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.12","value":"1Chr.11.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Merarite Levite, son of Mahli. Eleazar died without sons, so his daughters were married to their first cousins (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.23.21-22","r":"1Chr.23.21-22","rawR":"1Chr.23.21-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.23.21-22","value":"1Chr.23.21-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 23:21-22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.24.28","r":"1Chr.24.28","rawR":"1Chr.24.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.24.28","value":"1Chr.24.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"24:28"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Priest descended from Phinehas. This Eleazar helped inventory the temple treasure on returning from the exile with Ezra (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.8.33","r":"Ezra.8.33","rawR":"Ezra.8.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.8.33","value":"Ezra.8.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 8:33"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["6. Parosh’s son, listed with others who divorced their foreign wives in the reform under Ezra (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.25","r":"Ezra.10.25","rawR":"Ezra.10.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.25","value":"Ezra.10.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:25"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["7. Priest in attendance at the dedication of the rebuilt walls of Jerusalem following the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.42","r":"Neh.12.42","rawR":"Neh.12.42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.42","value":"Neh.12.42"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:42"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["8. Person in the lineage of Joseph, husband of Mary (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.1.15","r":"Matt.1.15","rawR":"Matt.1.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.1.15","value":"Matt.1.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 1:15"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Genealogy of Jesus Christ"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Eleazar","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ex 6:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.6.23","rawQueryValue":"Exod.6.23","sourceRefExact":"Exod.6.23"},{"anchorText":"Ex 28:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.28.1","rawQueryValue":"Exod.28.1","sourceRefExact":"Exod.28.1"},{"anchorText":"Lv 8:2, 13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.8.2,13","rawQueryValue":"Lev.8.2,13","sourceRefExact":"Lev.8.2,13"},{"anchorText":"Lv 10:1-7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.10.1-7","rawQueryValue":"Lev.10.1-7","sourceRefExact":"Lev.10.1-7"},{"anchorText":"Nm 3:1-4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.3.1-4","rawQueryValue":"Num.3.1-4","sourceRefExact":"Num.3.1-4"},{"anchorText":"Nm 3:32","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.3.32","rawQueryValue":"Num.3.32","sourceRefExact":"Num.3.32"},{"anchorT